      "title": "Start here",
      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "Note"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "ADACHI WORKBENCH — OFFICIAL EXAMPLE\n\n1. Select an installed checkpoint. Replace the placeholder with one installed checkpoint. Use a compatible standard image checkpoint with CLIP and VAE.\n\n2. Text to image: select the matching group preset, edit its prompts and image size, then Queue. SaveImage receives only the active branch.\n\n3. Inpaint: upload or drop an image into Inline Mask, paint a mask, select the Inpaint preset, and Queue. Or open the web workspace from Adachi Inpaint Workbench.\n\n4. Compare before and after in Image Compare. Adopt sends the chosen result back to the editor; the existing mask is preserved for the same region. Download a generated image to use it as a new source.\n\n5. Inline Mask also supports Crop + Blend. Choose a crop, paint inside it, generate, then blend the returned patch before applying. Hover over controls for shortcuts.\n\nOnly one preset branch must be enabled. Common switches, checkpoint loader and SaveImage stay outside both groups. No third-party node pack or LoRA is needed."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
